# L §6.1 Identities are written (tally 2.1.8, the user's cut, plan §13; #187): a scenario's version is a version of the
# model it is over, so its same between an observed row and a move instance is refused at load alike (LOAD-SAME).
=== base.tally
model hh
  tally 2
  on 2026-04-30
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source plan "plan"
source bk "bank"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
place konto: accounts PLN lives 2019-01-01..
place world: outside lives 1900-01-01..
input bank: observed
input amt: money PLN
input dom: int

move pay[m in months]: transfers
  on day_of(m, dom)
  at start_of(m)
  leg cash from konto to world amount amt

version v
  cite plan
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  amt = 100.00 PLN "plan"
  dom = 10 "plan"
  opening[konto] = 1 000.00 PLN at 2026-01-01 start "saldo"

version st
  cite bk
  governs 2026-03
  known 2026-04-02
  covers konto
  bank[r1] = (on: 2026-03-10, kind: transfers, leg cash from konto to world amount 100.00 PLN) "line 1"

ask b: bal(konto, 2026-03-31)
=== sc.tally
scenario sc over hh
  tally 2
  from 2026-01-01
  note "x"

version sv
  cite bk
  governs 2026-03
  known 2026-04-02
  same bank[r1] = pay[2026-03]

ask b_sc: bal(konto, 2026-03-31) in sc
=== expect
scenario sc: refused: LOAD-SAME same bank[r1] = pay[2026-03]: an observed row and a planned instance of one model; state fulfils on the row (sc.tally:10)
b: 700.00 PLN
  unfulfilled: pay[2026-01]
  unfulfilled: pay[2026-02]
  open: pay[2026-03]
  cut 2026-04-30
warning: WARN-NEGATIVE konto is below zero from 2026-11-10
